      "name": "What should I do if a tree falls on my house?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "First, make sure everyone is safe — stay away from the tree until you've assessed for power lines. If lines are involved, call FirstEnergy / Illuminating Company before approaching. Photograph everything before any cleanup begins. Tarp any roof breach to prevent water intrusion. Call your homeowners insurance claims line within 24 hours to open the claim. Call the Roubic emergency line at {{global.phone}} for tree extraction. Do not attempt DIY removal — storm-damaged trees have unpredictable spring tension and are the leading cause of tree-related fatalities nationally." }
