      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does homeowners insurance cover tree removal after a storm?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Generally yes, when a tree damages a covered structure (house, garage, certain fence types, vehicle in some scenarios). Insurance typically does NOT cover removal of a tree that fell without damaging anything, or routine removal of a healthy tree. Roubic provides documentation — photos, itemized work, species and DBH estimates — built into the storm-response workflow so your claim moves through cleanly." }
