      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How quickly can Roubic respond to a storm emergency?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "We aim for on-site within 2–4 hours for emergencies inside our primary service area (Auburn Township, Pepper Pike, Chagrin Falls, Moreland Hills, Solon, and the surrounding inner-ring suburbs), and typically 1–2 hours after hours for Tier 1 cities. After-hours and weekend response carries a 50% surcharge over scheduled rates. Tier 2 and Tier 3 markets receive priority but may have slightly longer mobilization times during major regional storm events." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does emergency tree service cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Emergency, after-hours, and weekend tree service carries a 50% surcharge over scheduled rates. Tree-on-structure removal typically runs $800–$5,000 depending on tree size, structure type, and extraction complexity. Full-property storm cleanup (multi-tree, branches, debris) runs $1,500–$10,000+. Most structural-damage storm work is partially or fully covered by homeowners insurance when a covered structure is damaged." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What if the tree is on a power line?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Call the utility (FirstEnergy / Illuminating Company) FIRST. Assume every downed line is energized until proven otherwise. We will not touch energized lines without utility clearance — that's not stubbornness, it's the life-safety standard for tree services. Once the utility de-energizes the line and clears the scene, we can extract the tree. The wait can be hours during a major regional storm; in the meantime, stay back at least the tree's height from any down line." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you work with insurance companies directly?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "We don't negotiate the claim on your behalf — that's between you and your adjuster. But we eliminate the documentation friction that causes most claim delays by providing a complete packet (photos, itemized work scope, species and DBH estimates) the morning after the job. Adjusters routinely tell our customers that the Roubic documentation packet is unusually clean compared to typical contractor invoices." }
