      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "If the tree is fully on the ground, not contacting any structure, not contacting any power line, and you have chainsaw experience plus appropriate PPE, sometimes yes — for small trees. Larger trees with spring-loaded limbs, leaning trees, hung trees, or any tree near power lines should always be left to professionals. Storm-damaged trees are the leading cause of tree-related fatalities in the US, and the most common scenario is a homeowner cutting into spring-loaded wood that whips back unexpectedly." }
